From af2ef23f123be5ce047d4d13accdff07be297761 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: athexweb3 <athexweb3@nirapod.org>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:38:07 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] armv8a: add the SHA-256 and SHA-512 instructions

SHA256H, SHA256H2, SHA256SU0, SHA256SU1 (FEAT_SHA256) and SHA512H,
SHA512H2, SHA512SU0, SHA512SU1 (FEAT_SHA512) are available as intrinsics.
Their destination is also their first source. The semantics follow the
Arm pseudocode, including the SHA256hash function shared by SHA256H and
SHA256H2.

A proof-only file, armv8a_simd_facts.v, states what they compute in the
terms of FIPS 180-4: SHA256H and SHA256H2 perform four SHA-256 rounds,
SHA512H, SHA512H2 and an element-wise addition perform two SHA-512 rounds,
and the schedule-update pairs compute the next message-schedule words.
The same statements are made about the instruction descriptions, which
fixes the role of each operand.

A known-answer test computes SHA-256 and SHA-512 digests of the FIPS
180-4 example messages (empty, "abc" and a two-block message) with these
instructions, and checks them against the published digests under the
semantics of the compiler.
